  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "2afbc43e-4f96-42b0-8202-232f17318401",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 320,
      "shortId": "KTPUY",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "confirm-dialog-as-layer",
      "title": "Convert the confirm dialog to a layer with hintable buttons",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Migration step 2 from the design. A modal that draws its buttons manually has no child subtree, so `collect_hint_targets` finds nothing and it shows no keycaps — against the project rule that every action is KeyHint-reachable. Do it the conformant way: `OverlayHost::open_modal` with a ViewNode body and actions, NOT a bespoke modal.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nClosed 2026-08-04 by a reconciliation pass — **the confirm prompt is already a layer, built the conformant way.**\n\n`heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs::open_modal(state, spec: ModalSpec, completion)` is the entry point, and its module doc records the shape this task demanded: \"a `Button` per `ModalAction` — each carrying the overlay's id\". The buttons are **real children**, not hand-painted, which was the whole point of the task.\n\nThe hint half is wired too: `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:2185` runs `heca_grid_ui::collect_hint_targets(layer.root.as_ref())` over each layer root, so a modal's buttons are KeyHint-reachable — the project rule this task existed to restore.\n\n`heca/src/chrome/palette.rs`'s module note confirms the migration landed: \"the right-click context menu + the destructive-confirm prompt are now host-owned overlay layers in `chrome::overlay` — `open_dropdown` / `open_modal` — not bespoke fields here.\"\n\n**Not re-verified visually.** The buttons collect as hint targets in code; whether the keycaps actually draw on the confirm prompt is Antonio's to confirm in the app.",
