  "createdAt": "2026-07-26T11:28:31.721Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-08-11T22:46:22.737Z",
  "handoff": "# ⚠️ UPDATE 2026-08-11 — read this first; everything below it is still accurate\n\n**This handoff is still valid.** Nothing in it names an API that has since been deleted. Three\ncorrections and one addition, then read on unchanged.\n\n## Its \"Still open\" list, corrected\n\n- **Item 2, `activate_pane` — half answered.** The question was whether \"focus this pane and release\n  whoever holds the keyboard\" should be given to `focus_pane` or added beside it. F004/P084/T399\n  answered the *peek* half: `workspaces.peek_selected` now **takes** the keyboard for its own dock\n  (guarded, because `focus_dock` aimed at the dock that already holds it is the way back out), and a\n  gesture carries the seating it was declared in, so it lands on the right placement. **Still open:**\n  the sidebar's *click* path is still `focus_pane` + `unfocus_dock` composed at the call site, and\n  `unfocus_dock` is still a no-op when a layer rather than a dock holds the keyboard. Antonio's\n  complaint stands: *\"not only the surface but RPC, widgets… We need a single action that does\n  that.\"*\n- **`FocusPaneThenAction` is now explicitly forbidden as an answer to anything.** It is\n  `pub(crate)`, so a plugin cannot construct it — `AGENTS.md` ⭐⭐ RULE ZERO's worked example. If\n  \"focus my container, then run my action\" is needed it gets a **name** a plugin can say.\n- **The hint-target registry is gone** (F004/P084/T399). Where this handoff describes the exposé's\n  buttons or rows being reachable by `prefix+/`, the mechanism is now `KeyHint::on_peek` collected\n  out of the laid-out tree — no registry, no id, no `InteractionIntent`. `HintTargetRegistry`,\n  `HintTargetId`, `Base::hint_target`, `named_press` and `ViewHintTargets` **do not exist**.\n\n## New under it since, and worth knowing before touching the exposé\n\n- **The PTY resize is paced** and the reader thread survives interrupted reads (F004/P084/T409).\n  A surface that resizes panes rapidly no longer risks killing their shells.\n- **A pane divider transfers space between its own two panes** (F004/P084/T413), so the exposé's\n  picture of a column is now stable under a resize rather than rescaling every pane in it.\n\n## T327's own state\n\nUnchanged: **the actions are built and the exposé works end to end**; exactly four things are left\n(zoom instead of fade · floating panes undrawn · `preferred_height` ignored · `x`/`X`/`d` to delete\nfrom the map). They are in T327's own description, which was corrected on 2026-08-11 — the line\nthere saying \"the actions have not started\" was stale and is now marked as such.\n\n---\n\n# P082 handoff — T327 is in-progress with four items left; the 2026-08-06 exposé record kept below\n\n## Why this was rewritten (2026-08-10)\n\n`T327` (`ShowLayer`/`HideLayer` on-demand layers → the first native exposé) is **still\nin-progress**, and **its own description still says \"work has not started\"** — which is stale: the\nactions half is done and the map works end to end. An in-progress task whose description contradicts\nreality is worse than one that is simply open, so the status is recorded here, at the top, and\n**everything below this section is the 2026-08-06 handoff kept verbatim** — the niri model, the\ndecisions Antonio overrode, and the traps are all still current.\n\n## T327 — what is left, exactly four things\n\n1. **Zoom in/out on open/close instead of the fade.** Antonio: *\"The animation in niri is zoom-in/out\n   not fade.\"* niri animates `zoom` from 1.0 (life size) to 0.5. `PaintCx` already has translate,\n   clip and opacity through one chokepoint, so a scale can ride the same path — but it must also\n   scale font sizes, radii and border widths. The `Fade` stays until then.\n2. **Floating panes are modelled but not drawn.** `ExposeFloating` already carries strip coordinates.\n3. **`preferred_height` is ignored** — panes take an equal share of their column.\n4. **`x` / `X` / `d` to delete a pane / column / workspace from the map.** Never built. The older\n   handoff said it needs an \"the overlay initiated it\" `ActionPolicy` arm and to ask first — but with\n   the coverage bug fixed (the map no longer declares `covers_content`) that may be unnecessary.\n   **Check before proposing a new policy variant.**\n\nThese four are independent of each other, so they can equally well become their own tasks — that is\nAntonio's call, not something to decide while resuming.\n\n## One thing that changed under it since 2026-08-06 (F004/P084/T400, 2026-08-10)\n\nThe exposé is a **modal** layer, and modal layers now behave differently in two ways worth knowing\nbefore touching it:\n\n- **A modal layer holds the keyboard.** `domain_for` (`heca/src/app/interaction.rs:212`) no longer\n  reports `Domain::Container` while one is up, and `handle_keyboard_input` (`heca/src/app/input.rs`)\n  no longer lets a key the layer declined drive the dock behind it. Both sit **after** the global\n  resolve, so `q` → `close_overlay` still works.\n- **Keyboard events route by focus**, and `CardGrid` now declares `focusable` + `focus_barrier` in\n  its own constructor for that reason — it moves a cursor with the keyboard, so it takes the\n  keyboard. A `Widget` intent still enters the focused region's subtree, which is how `Activate` and\n  `Dismiss` reach the grid through the `Overlay`.\n\nIts two tests in `heca/src/chrome/expose.rs` (`an_activate_reaches_the_grid_and_chooses_the_card_under_the_cursor`,\n`a_dismiss_reaches_the_grid_through_the_overlay`) still pass unchanged.\n\n---\n\n# ↓ The 2026-08-06 handoff, kept verbatim ↓\n\n## State\n\nBranch `feat/palette-modes`. Last commit `fc9c18b`. **1189 tests, clippy 0 warnings** (the only line\nis `block v0.1.6`'s future-incompat note, from a dependency).\n\n⚠️ *(2026-08-10 note: the \"nothing is committed\" warning that stood here is spent — that work was\ncommitted long since. The file list it named is left below because it still says which files the\nexposé work touched.)*\n\nModified: `config.default.toml`, `heca-config/src/settings.rs`, `heca-core/src/layout/{session,types}.rs`,\n`heca-grid-ui/src/{component,effects,lib}.rs`, `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/{button,card_grid,dialog,input,mod,row,scroll_region}.rs`,\n`heca-grid-ui/tests/{phase_a,prop_drift}.rs`, `heca-theme/src/theme.rs`, `heca-view/src/{build,lib}.rs`,\n`heca-view-realize/src/lib.rs`, `heca/src/app/{events,focus,interaction,lifecycle,mutations,render,startup}.rs`,\n`heca/src/app_state.rs`, `heca/src/chrome/{expose,layers,mod}.rs`, `heca/src/providers/workspaces/mod.rs`.\n\n## What this session changed, and why\n\n### The exposé (T327) — working end to end\n\n`prefix+Tab` opens it. Enter/Space/click choose a pane; Escape/`q`/`Ctrl+q` close it.\n\n**niri's model, read out of `src/layout/monitor.rs` (fetched from the repo, not guessed):**\n\n```rust\nfn workspace_size(zoom) = view_size * zoom          // a row IS the screen, scaled\nfn workspace_gap(zoom)  = view_size.h * 0.1 * zoom  // gap = a tenth of a screen\nstatic_offset = (view_size - ws_size) / 2\nfirst_ws_y    = -active_ws_idx * ws_height_with_gap\nzoom          = 1 - progress * (1 - zoom_setting)   // opens by zooming OUT from life size\n```\n\n⚠️ **Antonio overrode part of it after seeing it (2026-08-05): centre the CARD THE CURSOR IS ON, not\nthe workspace rectangle.** niri centres the rectangle; heca centres the selected pane, on both axes,\nunclamped (`overscroll(true)`), because *\"the selected pane is centered even if it is the leftmost\"*.\n**Do not \"restore fidelity\" to niri here** — it was built that way, shown to him, and rejected. The\n`RevealWindow` widget and `Component::reveal_rect` built for the rectangle model were **reverted**;\ndo not reintroduce them.\n\nSettled about the map:\n- **No workspace-name gutter.** A fixed label column pushed every strip inwards so a row stopped\n  lining up with the screen it pictures; niri labels nothing either.\n- Zoom and row gap come from `LayoutOptions.overview_scale` / `.overview_gap`, exposed as\n  `[settings] overview_zoom` (0.5, clamped 0.05–0.75) and `overview_gap` (0.1, a **fraction of a\n  screen height**). **Not constants in `expose.rs`** — he rejected that explicitly: *\"we create\n  reusable things, not hardcoded, and expose configuration.\"*\n- `center_focused_column` was already fully implemented in `heca-core` and merely unreachable. Now\n  wired: `[settings] center_focused_column = \"never\" | \"on_overflow\" | \"always\"`, **default `never`\n  (niri's)**, was `OnOverflow`. Because the map draws each row at that workspace's own `view_offset`,\n  the setting shows through the map with **no code in `expose.rs`**.\n- Panes in a column use `Spacing::Sm` between them (at this zoom the real gap is a hairline and three\n  stacked panes read as one striped box).\n- Frosted backdrop: the layer declares `LayerBackdrop::Frosted`; the renderer runs one blur pass over\n  the scene between the chrome pass and the layer pass. Strength is the theme's `overlay_frost_radius`\n  (24 logical px). **Not `appearance.blur`** — that knob's contract is \"every appearance default is\n  off\", and three config tests enforce it.\n- Dissolve on close: `Fade`, 0.14s. Eased scroll: `Eased`, τ = 0.09s.\n\n### Framework bugs found and fixed — the important part\n\n**1. Seven widgets hand-rolled raw-key activation.** *(2026-08-10: this whole mechanism was replaced\nagain by F004/P084/T400 — `deaf_to_raw_key` and `takes_raw_keys` are gone, and keyboard events now\nroute by focus. The history is kept because the failure it describes is the one the new model exists\nto prevent.)* `Row`, `Button`, `IconButton`, `BadgeButton`, `Checkbox`, `Choice`, `Item` each claimed\n`Enter`/`Space` in the **capture** phase with no focus check. Capture runs top-down, so in any list\nthe first one reached ate the key and returned `Handled::Yes`, stopping the walk before\n`Keymap::dispatch` could offer the resolved `Activate` intent. **That is why the exposé's Enter did\nnothing while the mouse worked.** Antonio: *\"you know who built it? NO. YOU.\"*\n\n**2. `Dialog::submit` synthesised `Event::Key { Enter }`** at its primary button, because nothing\ncould say \"activate this child\" through `dyn Component`. Added `Component::activate()` — the\n`button.click()` that was missing. `Button::fire()` is the one path for pointer, key and `activate`.\n\n**3. The exposé blocked its own focus.** `content_covered()` was `covers_content || modal`, and the\nexposé needs `modal` to receive keys (`top_modal_root_mut`), so it could not describe itself. That put\nthe app in `Domain::Overlay`, where `FocusPane` is refused. **Below the `Modal` band, coverage is now\n`covers_content` alone**; `Modal`-band layers still cover unconditionally so a dialog cannot get it\nwrong. The exposé registers `modal: true, covers_content: false`. **A dialog covers; a map does not.**\n\n**4. The keyboard did not follow the focus.** `focus_pane` deliberately changes which pane is active\nand *nothing else* (a peek focuses without leaving). The sidebar dispatches `focus_pane` **and**\n`unfocus_dock` (`providers/workspaces/mod.rs:466`). The map now sends\n`FocusPaneThenAction { pane_id, action: UnfocusDock }` then `ActivateAction(CloseOverlay)`.\n⚠️ Antonio is right that this is still wrong: *\"not only the surface but RPC, widgets… We need a\nsingle action that does that.\"* See \"Still open\".\n\n**5. The right-click menu never opened on a workspace row.** `nav_key_at`\n(heca-grid-ui/src/nav.rs:70) reads `Base::nav_key` and nothing else. Pane cards (`:944`) and columns\n(`:1032`) declare it; the workspace `DockFrame` pushed its key into `signals.row_nav` and never told\nthe widget. Fixed with `dock.nav_key(workspace_nav_key(ws_idx))`. **This is the bug that motivated\nT394/T395** — menu, mapping and items all existed; one missing declaration produced silence.\n\n**6. An overlay swallowed keys it ignored.** `app/events.rs` returned unconditionally after offering a\nkey to the top modal layer, so anything the surface had no use for died there — which is why `q`,\ncatalogued and bound to `close_overlay` beside `Escape`, did nothing while the map was up. It now\nconsumes only what was handled.\n\n### Widget capabilities added (all generic, all in grid-ui)\n\n- `ScrollRegion::reveal_align(RevealAlign::{Minimal, Center})` + `center_on` — **both** axes;\n  `ensure_visible` was vertical-only, so a horizontal strip could never follow its cursor.\n- `ScrollRegion::overscroll(bool)` — the view may pass the ends of its content.\n- `ScrollRegion::scrollbars(bool)` — removes the thumb **and** its reserved gutter.\n- `ScrollRegion::smooth_scroll(secs)` — a **pointer drag** snaps (it must track the finger); a\n  **wheel notch** eases (a discrete tenth-of-a-viewport step; applying it instantly is a jump).\n- `effects::Eased` and `effects::Fade` — in `effects.rs` beside `Flash`/`Attention`, where Antonio\n  said they belong. I first inlined the same maths in `ScrollRegion` and hand-rolled a third copy as a\n  countdown in `LayerRegistry`; he called it out.\n- `PaintCx::with_opacity(alpha, f)` — multiplicative, through one `emit()` chokepoint;\n  `fade_command` dims fill/border/glow/shadow separately.\n- `CardGrid::on_move`, `GridCell::hovered` (hover **moves** the cursor rather than raising a second\n  claim beside it), per-row `(column, cell)` memory, vertical nav falling through at a column's ends\n  and entering the next column at the edge you arrived from.\n- `Row::hovered()` is public.\n\n### Layers\n\n`LayerBackdrop::{Plain, Frosted}`, `Fade` on the layer, `DynamicLayer::is_active()` (visible **and**\nnot dissolving) gating coverage / top-modal / input, `remove()` waiting for the dissolve (`doomed`),\n`LayerRegistry::tick`, `frost_opacity()`.\n⚠️ **Adding the fade broke activation once**: a dissolving layer still reported `visible`, so it kept\ncovering the panes for 140ms and `FocusPane` was refused — `[heca] interaction: blocked intent from\nKeyboard`, three times. `is_active()` is the fix. **An exit animation must never let a surface hold\nonto input it has already given up.**\n\n### AppState\n\n`expose_cursor_per_ws: Vec<Option<PaneId>>` — the map's own highlight, per workspace, maintained\nbeside `last_visited_pane_per_ws` (grown on add, removed on delete, in the same three places).\nDeliberately **not** `last_visited_pane_per_ws`: moving a highlight around a map is *looking*, not\ngoing, and must not rewrite the focus history `prefix+i` and the sidebar's dim highlight read.\nWritten by `InteractionIntent::ExposeCursor { pane_id }` — allowed in every domain, since it touches\nno session state and the only time it can fire is while the map is up.\n\n## 🔴 Still open\n\n1. *(2026-08-10: T394 and T395 are both done; T400 replaced the input model again. See the P084\n   handoff.)*\n2. **`activate_pane`** — one action meaning \"this pane is now the one I'm working in\": focus it and\n   release whoever holds the keyboard, whether that is a dock or a layer. Today `focus_pane` +\n   `unfocus_dock` is composed at each call site (sidebar, exposé), and `unfocus_dock` is a **no-op\n   when the keyboard is held by a layer** rather than a dock. **Ask Antonio** whether to give\n   `focus_pane` that behaviour or add `activate_pane` beside it — `focus_pane` is deliberately the\n   peek-shaped primitive and something relies on that.\n3. **`x` / `X` / `d` to delete a pane / column / workspace from the map.** (T327, item 4 above.)\n4. **Zoom in/out on open/close instead of the fade.** (T327, item 1 above.)\n5. **Floating panes are modelled but not drawn.** (T327, item 2 above.)\n6. **`preferred_height` is ignored.** (T327, item 3 above.)\n7. **Hover border on `Row`** — it has a hover *tint* but no distinct border. Belongs in grid-ui.\n\n## Traps this session paid for — do not re-learn them\n\n- **`view_offset` is measured from the ACTIVE COLUMN, not the strip.** The viewport's strip position\n  is `view_pos()` = `column_x(active) + view_offset`. Reading the raw offset put the workspace\n  rectangle in the wrong place in every scrolled workspace. The float test hid it by standing on\n  column 0, where the two coincide; it now stands on column 1.\n- **An `Overlay` paints its whole panel into the scene's OVERLAY layer**, so its *base* layer is\n  empty. Gating the layer render pass on \"did the base layer draw anything\" skipped it entirely and\n  `prefix+Tab` showed nothing.\n- **Bounding two numbers separately does not bound their sum.** The map's position is the centring pad\n  plus the scroll offset; bounding each let them add up to pushing everything off screen — twice.\n  `clamp_visible` clamps the **final shift** so a quarter of the viewport's content always stays on.\n- **`grow` and `align_self` are different axes.** The strip needs `grow(1.0)` for the row's height and\n  `align_self(Start)` for its width (so it measures its columns and the region has slack). Carrying a\n  wrapper's values down left the cards **7px tall**; removing the grow collapsed them.\n- **`Length::Pct` inside a `ScrollRegion` can never overflow it**, so nothing scrolls.\n- **`flex_grow` does not divide a region** — a share is grow + a zero base size + `shrink`.\n- **A share always fills**, so sizing columns as shares made every workspace look equally full. Sizes\n  are real size × zoom.\n- **The layer must be rebuilt before showing** (`chrome::rebuild_named_layer`): content is structural;\n  a signal replaces a prop, never a child.\n- **heca's window colour is translucent by design** (frosted compositor) — an overlay painted with it\n  lets the app read straight through.\n\n## How Antonio works — read before writing a line\n\n- **He is discussing, not commissioning, until he says otherwise.** *\"when I ask to start a discussion\n  YOU DON'T HAVE TO WRITE.\"* Answer the question; wait for \"fix\" / \"go\" / \"implement\".\n- **Answer, don't narrate.** *\"tell me the ActionPolicy is blocking instead of writing tons of\n  ceremony.\"* Short, direct, then stop.\n- **Never commit unless asked.**\n- **PRE-FLIGHT before EVERY new UI type**, not once per task: which existing widget does this; if none,\n  widget (grid-ui) or component (`heca/src/components/`); which planner task covers it. Skipping it is\n  how the easing got inlined instead of going into `effects.rs`.\n- **N copies of a rule = a missing API. Fix the model, not the call site.** He rejected a hand-rolled\n  guard outright and made it move into `dispatch`.\n- **`heca-grid-ui` must not learn about the app.** Not `ViewNode`, not `AppState`, not `WmAction`.\n- **Use the existing policy/config systems; never hardcode.** He rejected `const ZOOM` sitting beside\n  `LayoutOptions.overview_scale`.\n- **He drives every visual check and finds what tests cannot.** Green tests found none of this\n  session's six regressions; his screenshots found all of them. **Do not claim it works.** When stuck,\n  make the code tell you — a headless dispatch test proved the exposé tree was fine and moved the hunt\n  to the app; one trace line showed the focus was already landing. Reach for those **first**, not\n  after three speculative fixes.\n- Plain English, no ceremony, no empty acknowledgements.",
